  <section id="technical" class="step">
    <p class="kicker">Technical reference · for operators</p>
    <h2>Exact commands and checks</h2>
    <p class="small">This section is for the person or agent operating the deployment. You do not need it to use the studio, and it is not the beginner path.</p>
    <h3>Deploy the studio from its own repository</h3>
    <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/loftwah/composer-media-studio
cd composer-media-studio
pnpm install
npx wrangler d1 create media-studio
npx wrangler r2 bucket create media-studio
# set database_id and the bucket in wrangler.jsonc, then:
pnpm migrate:remote
printf '%s' "$OWNER_PASSPHRASE" | npx wrangler secret put OWNER_PASSPHRASE
printf '%s' "$SESSION_SECRET" | npx wrangler secret put SESSION_SECRET
printf '%s' "$FAL_KEY" | npx wrangler secret put FAL_KEY
pnpm run deploy -- --migrate</code></pre>
    <p>Requires Node 22.23.5+, 24.22.3+ or 26.13.1+ on the 22/24/26 lines. <code>pnpm run deploy</code> refuses a dirty tree, a branch other than <code>main</code>, or an unpushed commit, runs the focused tests once, deploys, and fails unless the live <code>/healthz</code> revision equals the shipped commit. Expected output ends with <code>released &lt;sha&gt;</code> and <code>live: https://…/healthz</code>.</p>
    <h3>Check a live studio without the browser</h3>
    <pre><code>curl -s https://your-studio.example/healthz
# &#123;"ok":true,"revision":"&lt;40-char sha&gt;","bridge":true,...&#125;
curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%&#123;http_code&#125;\n' https://your-studio.example/api/state
# 401 signed out: private routes are enforced on the server</code></pre>
    <h3>What the routes do</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><code>POST /api/projects/:id/generations</code> — one paid request, one client request id.</li>
      <li><code>POST /api/projects/:id/compositions</code> — save an ordered manifest of takes and a bed.</li>
      <li><code>POST /api/projects/:id/compositions/:cid/render</code> — one bounded render job; <code>studio-assembly</code> or <code>studio-social</code>.</li>
      <li><code>GET /render-input/:assetId?p&amp;e&amp;s</code> — signed, thirty-minute, single-asset read for a render job only.</li>
      <li><code>GET /api/projects/:id/export</code> — project, prompts, lineage and costs without secrets.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Troubleshooting</h3>
    <dl class="faults">
      <div><dt>Release refused: working tree is not clean</dt><dd>Commit or stash your changes. The guard exists so the live revision matches a reviewable commit.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Migration fails on a foreign key</dt><dd>The parent table is referenced. Rebuild the parent, then the children, then drop the old parent; copy rows and restore self-references in a second pass.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Handoff rejected as expired</dt><dd>Seconds versus milliseconds. Normalise the unit; do not lengthen the token to hide it.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Render job stuck at "result unavailable"</dt><dd>Reconcile. It re-reads the same provider result. If the provider's own detail names an invalid input, fix the request shape — that is how the single-input 9:16 attempt was found.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Images binding error 9432 on the Oyster route</dt><dd>Legacy billing on that account. It blocks the host's reference fitter, not the studio's own reference variation. Enable Cloudflare Images or migrate billing, and label which route produced which result.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Video refused: AI Gateway could not fund this request</dt><dd>Nothing was charged. Add credit and retry the same request id.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Blank media card after publishing</dt><dd>Check the asset revision and its publications. Withdrawal revokes the page; hiding only removes the card.</dd></div>
